From beb99d60d3113d439c0955f6eaf039332103be9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 03:03:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] perf(eccvm): parallelise transcript scalar muls and MSM
 trace construction

- ECCVMTranscriptBuilder::compute_rows: the full scalar multiplications P * mul_scalar_full of every
  mul op do not depend on the VM state; compute them up front in parallel, the sequential pass only
  adds them into the MSM accumulator (23 ms -> 9 ms on transfer_1_recursions+private_fpc).
- ECCVMMSMMBuilder::compute_rows: every MSM starts from the offset generator and owns a disjoint range
  of rows and p1/p2/p3 trace entries, so both the projective trace pass and the slope pass run in
  parallel over MSMs. is_double_or_add becomes one byte per entry (std::vector<bool> packs bits into
  shared words). 23 ms -> 15 ms.

The group elements produced are the same; all of them are normalised to affine before use.
---
 .../src/barretenberg/eccvm/msm_builder.hpp    | 23 ++++++++--------
 .../barretenberg/eccvm/transcript_builder.hpp | 26 +++++++++++++------
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/barretenberg/cpp/src/barretenberg/eccvm/msm_builder.hpp b/barretenberg/cpp/src/barretenberg/eccvm/msm_builder.hpp
